Subject: [PATCH] Rename keyname() to keyseqname()

The key sequence namer added in 4.4 for where-is/describe-key is
called keyname(), which ncurses already declares in curses.h as
keyname(int).  Any TU that pulls in def.h after ttydef.h therefore
fails with "conflicting types for 'keyname'" wherever configure finds
ncurses/curses.h -- which is what openSUSE does.

Upstream fixed this the same way right after tagging 4.4.

Upstream-Commit: https://github.com/troglobit/mg/commit/a62108264e
--- a/src/cinfo.c
+++ b/src/cinfo.c
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@
  * The names of the n keys in keys, space separated.
  */
 void
-keyname(char *buf, size_t len, const KCHAR *keys, int n)
+keyseqname(char *buf, size_t len, const KCHAR *keys, int n)
 {
 	char	*cp = buf;
 	int	 i;
--- a/src/def.h
+++ b/src/def.h
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@
 
 /* cinfo.c */
 char		*getkeyname(char  *, size_t, int);
-void		 keyname(char *, size_t, const KCHAR *, int);
+void		 keyseqname(char *, size_t, const KCHAR *, int);
 
 /* syntax.c */
 #define SYN_NONE	0
--- a/src/echo.c
+++ b/src/echo.c
@@ -1387,7 +1387,7 @@
